   "text": "I read the macrocycle as a cyclic peptide-like ring and traced it residue by residue, starting from the 4-CF3-phenylalanine at the top and going clockwise.\n\n**Ring sequence, clockwise from the top:**\n1. 4-CF3-Phe C\u03b1, bearing the CH2\u2013C6H4\u2013CF3 side chain (wedge). Its nitrogen belongs to the eight-membered lactam (azocan-2-one) at upper left.\n2. C(=O)\u2013N(Me)\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O): an N-methylglycine unit.\n3. NH\u2013CH(CH2CH2\u2013Ar\u2032)\u2013C(=O), where Ar\u2032 is 3,5-difluoro-4-CF3-phenyl (wedge at the C\u03b1).\n4. 4,4-Difluoropyrrolidine-2-carbonyl (proline-type), with its C\u03b1 wedged.\n5. NH\u2013C(cyclopentane, spiro)\u2013C(=O): a 1-aminocyclopentane-1-carbonyl unit.\n6. N(Me)\u2013CH(cyclopentyl)\u2013C(=O) (wedge).\n7. N(Me)\u2013CH(C(=O)NMe2)\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O): an N-methyl-aspartic dimethylamide unit, with the amide drawn on a hash.\n8. N(Me)\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013C(=O): N-methylalanine, with the methyl on a hash.\n9. NH\u2013CH(sec-butyl)\u2013C(=O): isoleucine, with a wedge at the C\u03b1 and the \u03b2-methyl wedged.\n10. N(Me)\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O): a second N-methylglycine unit.\n11. N(Me) on the lactam CH, which sits next to the lactam C=O. The ring is N, C=O, CH and five CH2, so eight atoms, and the CH\u2013CH2 bond is hashed.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned each wedged or hashed centre from its drawn geometry and converted it to @/@@ in the order the atoms appear in the SMILES. I did this by hand and did not run it through a toolkit.\n\nSMILES: FC(F)(F)c1ccc(cc1)C[C@H]2C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCc4cc(F)c(C(F)(F)F)c(F)c4)C(=O)N5CC(F)(F)C[C@H]5C(=O)NC6(CCCC6)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C7CCCC7)C(=O)N(C)[C@H](C(=O)N(C)C)CC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N(C)[C@H]3CCCCCN2C3=O"
